In the early afternoon, it is still very warm.
Suddenly, the sky turns dark.
Then it immediately starts to rain.
It is a really heavy summer rain.
Now the people at the flea market have to be fast.
The vendors quickly throw plastic sheets over their tables.
I run to a large tree.
Here under the tree, I stay dry.
I think about a terrible storm three months ago.
Three months ago, the rain was still icy.
Back then, I was terribly cold outside.
But this summer rain is completely different.
This air today is wonderfully warm.
Normally I don't like rain, but this rain is nice.
Everything suddenly smells so good and fresh.
Some people run laughing across the square.
But it is still raining very hard.
I will soon need a better place to wait.
